    "chunk_size_bytes": 970,
    "chunk_text": "Probe illegal online advertising by betting centers\n\nColombo, June 17 (Daily Mirror) - Committee on Public Finance (COPF) has directed the Telecommunication Regulatory Commission (TRC) and other relevant institutions to carry out a probe on illegal online advertising by betting centres, it was revealed yesterday.\n\n\u201cOnline betting sites are advertising openly across Sri Lanka with zero regulations. How could this be allowed?\u201d COPF Chief Harsha de Silva questioned.\n\n\u201cI questioned the relevant officials on this massive legal blind spot and billions of tax revenue bleeding from the State,\u201d Dr. De Silva said in his latest social media post.\n\n\u201cI see online advertisements even carrying the official government logo. I cannot be silent about the issue,\u201d MP de Silva had told the relevant government officials during the recent COPF meeting.\n\nHe said he will issue a directive to the relevant institutions to look into the matter and submit a report to COPF."
