    "chunk_text": "The MSD have highlighted that the move is necessary due to potential risks associated with the devices, including complications that could arise during or after cardiac procedures. Medical professionals have been advised to closely monitor patients who have already received the stents, as part of ongoing clinical safety surveillance.\n\nMeanwhile, discussions are continuing within the medical community over the need for a full investigation into how the stents were approved and distributed. Health officials have not yet confirmed whether further batches or related devices may also be reviewed, leaving the situation under close observation.\n\nFor now, hospitals remain on high alert as they work to remove the affected devices and ensure uninterrupted cardiac care services, while authorities stress that patient safety remains the top priority.\n\nThe controversy has intensified after Chairman of the Doctors' Trade Union Alliance for Medical and Civil Rights, Specialist Dr. Chamal Sanjeewa publicly called for a comprehensive investigation into the incident. He urged the Health Secretary to immediately disclose whether any patient deaths have occurred due to complications linked to the stents. His statement has added pressure on health authorities to provide clearer answers and publish full clinical findings.\n\nDr. Sanjeewa also requested that authorities conduct a transparent probe into how the stents entered the national supply chain and whether proper quality checks were followed before distribution to hospitals. His comments reflect growing concern within parts of the medical community about regulatory oversight and patient safety safeguards."
