    "chunk_text": "The new mould should facilitate the flow of resources to activities that will reduce poverty The State should provide all of this as a part of their economic plans for the country. There is need to be ruthless. If there is a foreign exchange cost, and if this could be found only by stopping the imports of cars, this should be done until adequate funds are available.\n\nRevitalizing villages could also be a route to generate exports.\n\nTo develop anything investment is essential. It is investment that makes the wheels turn and converts poverty to prosperity. The heartland of our country comprises thousands of villages. If we have prosperous villages we will have a prosperous country . Why didn\u2019t we have large scale investment that would have created the essential infrastructure vital to create growth? We were able to find the funds and have major investments, but they did not help to develop the country. But they perhaps benefited those who initiated these investments that had no impact on developing the country\n\nMetaphorically speaking China dangled a lollipop. They invested USD 1.4 billion to reclaim 269 ha of land from the sea off Galle Face (Colombo Port City), the title for which was retained by the Government of Sri Lanka), in return for a 99-year lease of 116 ha of the reclaimed land.\n\nAfter number of sessions of waving the lollipop under our nose we agreed and said yes to the proposal of reclaiming land from the sea and giving China a 99-year lease on part of the reclaimed land. The reclamation was concluded by the China Harbour Engineering Corporation (CHEC). Both our and the Chinese share of the reclaimed land remained idle for years. Now a grand package of tax and other benefits has attracted a few investors who plan to build apartments and commercial space on this prime reclaimed land."
