    "chunk_text": "Erhambaram, With the experience he had working under Dr. V.S. Ramanathan tried to practice medicine and his son Umakanthan succeeded him. Later when unrest started in Jaffna, Umakanthan with the help of the LTTE remained in the hospital. As mentioned already, Mr. C.V.K. Sivagnanam was the Commissioner of the Municipality picked by the LTTE.\n\nIn 1977 My father started a DC case asking for a new Board for the hospital. Five trustees were appointed. Umakanthan was asked to hand over the keys of the hospital to my mother. He vanished with the keys.\n\nIn 1993 or 1994, the Hospital was targeted by aerial bombing. But luckily the bomb did not hit the hospital. Umakanthan took full control."
