    "md5": "1ddf1d7ba0dda4df1217562662edad9b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1693,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s enterprise leaders chart course for secure AI adoption at Innovation Forum 2026\n\nAligned with Sri Lanka\u2019s National Digital Economy Strategy 2030, the IBM Innovation Forum Sri Lanka 2026 brought together senior business leaders, technology decision-makers, and government representatives to chart a practical path for enterprise AI adoption. Held on June 5 at The Studio, Cinnamon Life City of Dreams, the flagship event explored how organisations can move beyond experimentation to operationalise AI securely and at scale.\n\nUnder the theme \u201cBuilding Secure, AI-Driven, and Autonomous Enterprises in Sri Lanka,\u201d the forum featured in-depth discussions on cybersecurity, infrastructure modernisation, data protection, operational resilience, and governance. Industry experts emphasised that Sri Lankan enterprises are entering a defining phase where technology investments must translate into measurable business outcomes.\n\nCem Borhan, CEO \u2013 ASEAN & South Asia, Redington, noted that the collaboration with IBM reflects a shared commitment to helping enterprises innovate responsibly and unlock long-term growth. \u201cThrough the IBM Innovation Forum, we are bringing together leaders from across government, industry, and technology to exchange insights and enable practical pathways for AI-driven transformation,\u201d he said.\n\nSri Lanka and Russia forge path to enhanced tourism ties at Moscow Forum\n\nCSE opens trading floor to public as investor forum showcases 360% market growth\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
