    "chunk_text": "University of West London opens Sri Lanka Branch Campus\n\nSeated from left: CEG Holdings and ANC Education Chairman Dr. Jagath Alwis, University of West London Vice Chancellor and President Professor Peter John CBE and Ceylinco Holdings PLC Executive Chairman and CEO Ajith Gunawardena\n\nStanding from left: ANC Campus CEO Dayan Fernando, The UK Trade Envoy to Sri Lanka Lord Hannett of Everton, British High Commissioner to Sri Lanka Andrew Patrick and ANC Education Executive Director Dr. Punarjeeva Karunanayake\n\nNewly established University of West London Sri Lanka Campus in Colombo\n\nThe University of West London (UWL) formally opened the University of West London Sri Lanka Branch Campus, the country\u2019s first full UK university branch campus, marking a landmark development in Sri Lanka\u2019s higher education sector.\n\nThe University of West London Sri Lanka Branch Campus is designed to bring a UK university learning experience closer to the students in Sri Lanka. The campus is operated by ANC Campus, a pioneer in the higher education sector in Sri Lanka, with over two decades of experience in delivering internationally recognised education.\n\nThe University of West London Sri Lanka Branch Campus gives the students the opportunity to study towards world-class UK degrees while remaining close to home. Academic delivery, assessment and quality assurance will be aligned with the UWL standards, with the university maintaining academic oversight of its courses and awards.\n\nThe students will have access to the UWL-approved programmes, academic support, learning resources and a campus environment designed to promote academic success, confidence and employability."
