    "chunk_size_bytes": 1659,
    "chunk_text": "The University of West London Sri Lanka Branch Campus gives the students the opportunity to study towards world-class UK degrees while remaining close to home. Academic delivery, assessment and quality assurance will be aligned with the UWL standards, with the university maintaining academic oversight of its courses and awards.\n\nThe students will have access to the UWL-approved programmes, academic support, learning resources and a campus environment designed to promote academic success, confidence and employability.\n\nCEG Holdings and ANC Campus Chairman Dr. Jagath Alwis said, \u201cFor students and parents, the financial advantage is one of the most significant benefits. Studying locally can substantially reduce the overall cost of obtaining a UK university degree by eliminating many of the major expenses associated with studying overseas, including accommodation in London, living expenses, airfares, visa-related charges, Immigration Health Surcharge, accommodation deposits and relocation costs.\n\nAt its inception, the UWL Sri Lanka Branch Campus will offer programmes in business, IT, law, AI, psychology and early childhood education, subject to applicants meeting the UWL entry requirements. Professional accreditations or recognitions, where applicable, will be communicated through the official UWL-approved programme information.\u201d\n\nThe UWL is recognised as the Best Modern University in London in The Times and The Sunday Times Good University Guide 2026, No. 1 London university for overall student satisfaction in the National Student Survey 2025 and a Top 5 UK university for student experience in the Daily Mail University Guide 2026."
