    "chunk_size_bytes": 1787,
    "chunk_text": "The inaugural flight marks another milestone in FitsAir\u2019s network expansion strategy. As Sri Lanka\u2019s first privately-owned airline, this reinforces its commitment to enhancing regional connectivity through affordable travel. A special launch ceremony was held to commemorate the occasion, attended by representatives from FitsAir, the travel trade, tourism sector, Walker\u2019s Tours, Cinnamon Hotels & Resorts, and Cinnamon Life City of Dreams.\n\nSpeaking at the launch, FitsAir Executive Director Ammar Kassim highlighted that routes transcend airports by connecting dreams, driving trade, and building partnerships.\n\nThe introduction of this direct route significantly alters the competitive landscape for air travel between Colombo and Ahmedabad. Prior to this launch, passengers had to rely on indirect, one-stop flights operated by competitors such as IndiGo and SriLankan Airlines. IndiGo has traditionally served this route with layovers in major Indian cities such as Chennai, Mumbai, Bengaluru, and Hyderabad, resulting in total travel times ranging from seven to over twelve hours depending on the connection. Similarly, SriLankan Airlines has offered indirect options, often involving layovers in New Delhi.\n\nBy eliminating the need for layovers, FitsAir\u2019s direct service drastically reduces the journey time to approximately three hours and forty minutes, compared to the eight hours or more typically required on competing indirect routes. This time-saving advantage positions FitsAir highly favourably against IndiGo and SriLankan Airlines, especially for business travellers and tourists seeking quick short-haul getaways. While competitors may still compete on frequency and network reach through their hubs, FitsAir holds a distinct monopoly on the non-stop segment."
  },
