    "chunk_text": "If Sri Lanka is to emerge from its historical economic hardships and build a stable future, it must unleash the creative energy of its youth. Entrepreneurship is not merely an alternative business path; it is the vital spinal cord required to support a modern, self-reliant economy. By dismantling bureaucratic barriers, reforming education, and rewriting financial rules, the nation can transform an underemployed generation into a dynamic force of self-starters ensuring that the country never again has to compromise its future on the altar of fiscal mismanagement."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2026-06-22-colombotelegraphcom-7f347c4f",
    "num": "colombotelegraphcom-7f347c4f",
