    "md5": "04cb941b27a07cf273afaba15b5aabbf",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1817,
    "chunk_text": "Veepee Graphics Lanka participates at  Sri Lanka Print and Trade Fair Exhibition 2026\n\nVeepee Graphics Lanka Director Nalani Madhushani, Industries Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara and Sri Lanka United National Business Alliance Chairman Tania Abeysundara lighting the traditional oil lamp to inaugurate the Veepee stall\n\nVeepee Graphics Lanka, a premier prepress and premedia organisation, showcased itself at the Sri Lanka Print and Trade Fair Exhibition 2026 at the BMICH.\n\nIts stall was ceremoniously inaugurated with a ribbon-cutting ceremony and the lighting of the traditional oil lamp by Veepee Graphics Lanka Director Nalani Madhushani, Industries Ministry Secretary Thilaka Jayasundara, and Sri Lanka United National Business Alliance Chairman Tania Abeysundara. Sri Lanka Association of Printers President Eng. Janaka Rathnakumara also participated in the momentous occasion. The exhibition, recognised as Sri Lanka\u2019s premier and largest printing, packaging, labelling, signage, and graphic communications event, concluded on Sunday serving as a prime platform for the company to showcase its cutting-edge innovations in the flexible packaging sector.\n\n\u200bOperating as a proud extension of Bangalore-based Veepee Graphic Solutions, Veepee Graphics Lanka has established itself as a trusted name synonymous with quality, precision, and technological excellence. The strategic initiative to expand into Sri Lanka was positioned by astute entrepreneur P. Jaichandra. Today, the organisation is further strengthened by its future-ready leadership, with Natasha Jaichandra representing the next generation. As one of the youngest directors in the flexible packaging industry, she brings youthful energy, technical acumen, and a progressive vision that seamlessly blends tradition with modern innovation."
  },
