    "chunk_size_bytes": 1842,
    "chunk_text": "Veepee Graphics Lanka opens high-tech  stall at Print & Trade Fair Exhibition\n\nVeepee Graphics Lanka Director Nalani Madhushani, Secretary to the Ministry of Industries Thilaka Jayasundara, Chairman of the Sri Lanka United National Business Alliance Tania Abeysundara, and Sri Lanka Association of Printers President Eng. Janaka Rathnakumara participating in the ribbon-cutting ceremony\n\n\u200bVeepee Graphics Lanka officially opened its stall at the Sri Lanka Print & Trade Fair Exhibition 2026 at the BMICH.\n\nThe stall was inaugurated with a ribbon-cutting ceremony and the lighting of the traditional oil lamp by Veepee Graphics Lanka Director Nalani Madhushani, Secretary to the Ministry of Industries Thilaka Jayasundara, and Chairman of the Sri Lanka United National Business Alliance Tania Abeysundara. Sri Lanka Association of Printers President Eng. Janaka Rathnakumara also participated in the occasion.\n\nThe exhibition, recognized as Sri Lanka\u2019s premier and largest printing, packaging, labelling, signage, and graphic communications event, runs from June 19 to 21, serving as a prime platform for the company to showcase its cutting-edge innovations in the flexible packaging sector.\n\n\u200bOperating as a proud extension of Bangalore-based Veepee Graphic Solutions, Veepee Graphics Lanka has established itself as a trusted name synonymous with quality, precision, and technological excellence.\n\nThe strategic initiative to expand into Sri Lanka was positioned by astute entrepreneur P. Jaichandra. Today, the organization is further strengthened by its future-ready leadership, with Natasha Jaichandra representing the next generation. As one of the youngest directors in the flexible packaging industry, she brings youthful energy, technical acumen, and a progressive vision that seamlessly blends tradition with modern innovation."
  },
